      "topics": [],
      "fastest": true,
      "reverse": false,
      "shortest": true,
      "solution": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\nint main() {\n    char s[11];\n    scanf(\"%s\", s);\n\n    int o = 0, c = 0, n = strlen(s);\n\n    if (n % 2) return puts(\"-1\"), 0;\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)\n        if (s[i] == '{')\n            o++;\n        else if (o)\n            o--;\n        else\n            c++;\n\n    printf(\"%d\", (o + 1) / 2 + (c + 1) / 2);\n}",
      "statement": "Given a string consisting only of characters {{{}} and {{}}}, determine the minimum number of bracket reversals required to make the string balanced.\nA reversal changes:\n\n{{{}} into {{}}}\n{{}}} into {{{}}\n\nA string is balanced if:\n\nEvery opening bracket has a matching closing bracket.\nWhile reading the string from left to right, the number of closing brackets never exceeds the number of opening brackets.\nThe total number of opening and closing brackets is equal.\n\nExamples:\n\n{{{{}}}} is balanced.\n}}{{ is not balanced.\n{{}{ is not balanced.\n\nIf it is impossible to balance the string, output {{-1}}.",
